xnu 0484: start the wifi worker when the gadget threads exist

Measured 2026-11-26: `wifistage 1` on 0481-0483 while `wifistage` itself
answered. The command thread is created inside `mondrian_usb_gadget_start()`,
so a live command channel with a missing worker means `mondrian_usb_probe()`
never returns -- it stops in the eUSB2 read block that follows the gadget
start, and the block-level `mondrian_wifi_start()` is never reached.

The worker now starts immediately after `mondrian_usb_gadget_start()`, before
the eUSB2 block. Every window it uses is premapped by `mondrian_wifi_premap()`
on the boot thread, and the remaining probe code only reads pages that are
already mapped.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 4c8bd7a..fe2fb0f 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -2402,7 +2402,6 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		extern void mondrian_spmi_probe(void);
 		extern void mondrian_reset_reason_init(void);
 		extern void mondrian_wifi_premap(void);
-		extern void mondrian_wifi_start(void);
 
 		/*
 		 * The premap takes every window the wifi worker touches before
@@ -2417,15 +2416,6 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		(void)mondrian_gpu_probe();
 		mondrian_touch_probe();
 		mondrian_usb_probe();
-		/*
-		 * Start here, before the audio/Venus/BT tail: the block has been
-		 * measured to stop in that tail when the pin premap runs first
-		 * (0481/0482: `wifistage 1`, the worker never reached stage 2),
-		 * while starting inside `usb_probe` reached `worker started`
-		 * (0480). Every window the worker uses is premapped above, so it
-		 * takes no ml_io_map() and cannot race the tail.
-		 */
-		mondrian_wifi_start();
 		mondrian_audio_probe_start();
 		mondrian_venus_start();
 		mondrian_bt_tty_init();
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c
index 332b2fb..702775b 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c
@@ -243,6 +243,19 @@ mondrian_usb_probe(void)
 		    usb_rd(dwc, DWC3_GUCTL), usb_rd(dwc, DWC3_GUCTL1));
 		if (usb >= 2) {
 			mondrian_usb_gadget_start(dwc);
+			/*
+			 * The gadget threads (events, log, commands) exist from here
+			 * on, and the rest of this probe only reads windows that are
+			 * already mapped. The block that follows this function has
+			 * been measured to stop before its `mondrian_wifi_start()`
+			 * call (0481-0483: `wifistage 1` while `wifistage` answered),
+			 * so the worker starts here, before the eUSB2 read block.
+			 */
+			{
+				extern void mondrian_wifi_start(void);
+
+				mondrian_wifi_start();
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
